## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Astro project.

### Changes Made:

**1. Package Installation:**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.x)
- Updated `package.json` with new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect new dependency

**2. Analytics Integration in Layout:**
- Modified `src/layouts/Layout.astro`
- Added import statement: `import Analytics from '@vercel/analytics/astro'`
- Inserted `<Analytics />` component in the `<head>` section
- Placed before theme initialization script to ensure early loading

**3. Implementation Details:**
- Followed official Vercel documentation retrieved from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used Astro-specific Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/astro`
- Component placed in the main Layout.astro file to track all pages
- Analytics will automatically begin collecting data once deployed to Vercel

**4. Verification:**
- Build completed successfully with no errors
- All 8 pages built correctly (homepage, about, blog posts, work, 404)
- No TypeScript or linting errors introduced

### Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Locked dependency versions
- `src/layouts/Layout.astro` - Added Analytics component

### Next Steps:
Once deployed to Vercel, analytics will automatically start tracking:
- Page views
- Visitor data
- Performance metrics

The analytics dashboard will be available in the Vercel project settings.
